{"video_id": "2xUxDkEtdio", "channel_id": "UCTGVey70JGK1SRQtJMy153g", "fetched_at": "2026-11-17T03:19:30.341615+00:00", "fetch_tool": "yt-dlp 2026.08.19", "caption_track_type": "auto_generated", "segments": [{"start_seconds": 0.0, "end_seconds": 4.48, "text": "A model is only as good as the way you"}, {"start_seconds": 2.16, "end_seconds": 6.36, "text": "measure it. By the end, you'll know how"}, {"start_seconds": 4.48, "end_seconds": 8.64, "text": "to tell whether a strong-looking score"}, {"start_seconds": 6.36, "end_seconds": 11.24, "text": "represents real predictive performance"}, {"start_seconds": 8.64, "end_seconds": 14.76, "text": "or an evaluation mistake. A model can"}, {"start_seconds": 11.24, "end_seconds": 17.28, "text": "report 95% accuracy and still be useless"}, {"start_seconds": 14.76, "end_seconds": 18.48, "text": "when 95% of the data belongs to one"}, {"start_seconds": 17.28, "end_seconds": 20.52, "text": "class."}, {"start_seconds": 18.48, "end_seconds": 22.56, "text": "The same number becomes meaningless if"}, {"start_seconds": 20.52, "end_seconds": 25.2, "text": "the model was evaluated on its training"}, {"start_seconds": 22.56, "end_seconds": 27.36, "text": "data. And for time-dependent data,"}, {"start_seconds": 25.2, "end_seconds": 30.2, "text": "randomly shuffling before the split can"}, {"start_seconds": 27.36, "end_seconds": 32.36, "text": "let future information predict the past."}, {"start_seconds": 30.2, "end_seconds": 35.16, "text": "The payoff is a reliable evaluation"}, {"start_seconds": 32.36, "end_seconds": 37.44, "text": "strategy. Separate training, validation,"}, {"start_seconds": 35.16, "end_seconds": 39.76, "text": "and testing. Rotate validation with"}, {"start_seconds": 37.44, "end_seconds": 41.88, "text": "cross-validation. Select metrics that"}, {"start_seconds": 39.76, "end_seconds": 44.48, "text": "reflect the cost of mistakes. And read"}, {"start_seconds": 41.88, "end_seconds": 46.36, "text": "learning curves for bias and variance."}, {"start_seconds": 44.48, "end_seconds": 48.6, "text": "You'll also see why leakage, class"}, {"start_seconds": 46.36, "end_seconds": 50.32, "text": "imbalance, and repeated test set checks"}, {"start_seconds": 48.6, "end_seconds": 51.68, "text": "can make a bad model look ready for"}, {"start_seconds": 50.32, "end_seconds": 53.84, "text": "production."}, {"start_seconds": 51.68, "end_seconds": 56.36, "text": "Reliable evaluation begins with three"}, {"start_seconds": 53.84, "end_seconds": 59.32, "text": "data sets and three distinct purposes."}, {"start_seconds": 56.36, "end_seconds": 61.68, "text": "The training set, commonly 60% to 70%"}, {"start_seconds": 59.32, "end_seconds": 65.12, "text": "here, contains examples the model learns"}, {"start_seconds": 61.68, "end_seconds": 68.08, "text": "from. The validation set, commonly 15%"}, {"start_seconds": 65.12, "end_seconds": 70.4, "text": "to 20%, supports hyperparameter tuning"}, {"start_seconds": 68.08, "end_seconds": 72.6, "text": "and model selection. The model doesn't"}, {"start_seconds": 70.4, "end_seconds": 75.12, "text": "train on those examples, but validation"}, {"start_seconds": 72.6, "end_seconds": 79.0, "text": "results influence your decisions."}, {"start_seconds": 75.12, "end_seconds": 81.0, "text": "The test set, also commonly 15% to 20%,"}, {"start_seconds": 79.0, "end_seconds": 82.72, "text": "is reserved for the final model and"}, {"start_seconds": 81.0, "end_seconds": 84.88, "text": "touched exactly once to report"}, {"start_seconds": 82.72, "end_seconds": 87.0, "text": "performance. If you inspect test"}, {"start_seconds": 84.88, "end_seconds": 89.36, "text": "performance and then change the model,"}, {"start_seconds": 87.0, "end_seconds": 91.96, "text": "that set is no longer a test set. It has"}, {"start_seconds": 89.36, "end_seconds": 93.88, "text": "become another validation set."}, {"start_seconds": 91.96, "end_seconds": 95.84, "text": "This separation creates the holdout"}, {"start_seconds": 93.88, "end_seconds": 98.08, "text": "guarantee. The final reported"}, {"start_seconds": 95.84, "end_seconds": 101.16, "text": "performance reflects behavior on truly"}, {"start_seconds": 98.08, "end_seconds": 103.68, "text": "unseen data. Fit on training data, tune"}, {"start_seconds": 101.16, "end_seconds": 105.8, "text": "through validation, finalize the model,"}, {"start_seconds": 103.68, "end_seconds": 108.48, "text": "and only then cross the last boundary to"}, {"start_seconds": 105.8, "end_seconds": 110.84, "text": "the test set. A single train-validation"}, {"start_seconds": 108.48, "end_seconds": 113.08, "text": "split can waste data and produce a noisy"}, {"start_seconds": 110.84, "end_seconds": 115.88, "text": "estimate, especially with a small data"}, {"start_seconds": 113.08, "end_seconds": 118.6, "text": "set. K-fold cross-validation rotates the"}, {"start_seconds": 115.88, "end_seconds": 120.49, "text": "validation role across the data. Start"}, {"start_seconds": 118.6, "end_seconds": 123.29, "text": "by dividing the data set into K"}, {"start_seconds": 120.49, "end_seconds": 125.93, "text": "equal-sized folds. For each rotation,"}, {"start_seconds": 123.29, "end_seconds": 127.89, "text": "train on K minus one folds and validate"}, {"start_seconds": 125.93, "end_seconds": 130.37, "text": "on the remaining fold."}, {"start_seconds": 127.89, "end_seconds": 132.45, "text": "Then average the K validation scores."}, {"start_seconds": 130.37, "end_seconds": 134.77, "text": "Every data point serves as validation"}, {"start_seconds": 132.45, "end_seconds": 137.21, "text": "exactly once, while also participating"}, {"start_seconds": 134.77, "end_seconds": 140.89, "text": "in training during the other rotations."}, {"start_seconds": 137.21, "end_seconds": 143.17, "text": "K = 5 and K = 10 are standard choices in"}, {"start_seconds": 140.89, "end_seconds": 145.97, "text": "the lesson. The average is more stable"}, {"start_seconds": 143.17, "end_seconds": 148.37, "text": "than the result from any single split."}, {"start_seconds": 145.97, "end_seconds": 150.73, "text": "The discipline matters. Each fold must"}, {"start_seconds": 148.37, "end_seconds": 152.61, "text": "use the same evaluation procedure, and"}, {"start_seconds": 150.73, "end_seconds": 154.53, "text": "candidate models should be compared on"}, {"start_seconds": 152.61, "end_seconds": 155.73, "text": "identical folds and pre-processing"}, {"start_seconds": 154.53, "end_seconds": 157.93, "text": "pipelines."}, {"start_seconds": 155.73, "end_seconds": 160.29, "text": "Otherwise, differences caused by data"}, {"start_seconds": 157.93, "end_seconds": 163.17, "text": "selection or pre-processing noise can be"}, {"start_seconds": 160.29, "end_seconds": 165.45, "text": "mistaken for differences between models."}, {"start_seconds": 163.17, "end_seconds": 167.65, "text": "Basic K-fold rotates the holdout, but"}, {"start_seconds": 165.45, "end_seconds": 170.53, "text": "imbalanced classification needs another"}, {"start_seconds": 167.65, "end_seconds": 173.45, "text": "constraint. Stratified K-fold preserves"}, {"start_seconds": 170.53, "end_seconds": 176.33, "text": "the class distribution inside each fold."}, {"start_seconds": 173.45, "end_seconds": 179.05, "text": "If the full data set is 70% class A and"}, {"start_seconds": 176.33, "end_seconds": 181.05, "text": "30% class B, every fold should keep"}, {"start_seconds": 179.05, "end_seconds": 183.33, "text": "roughly that ratio."}, {"start_seconds": 181.05, "end_seconds": 185.45, "text": "Without stratification, a random split"}, {"start_seconds": 183.33, "end_seconds": 188.09, "text": "can place too few minority examples in a"}, {"start_seconds": 185.45, "end_seconds": 190.49, "text": "validation fold, or even concentrate all"}, {"start_seconds": 188.09, "end_seconds": 192.53, "text": "minority samples in one fold. That"}, {"start_seconds": 190.49, "end_seconds": 193.97, "text": "creates unstable scores and weak"}, {"start_seconds": 192.53, "end_seconds": 196.77, "text": "evidence about minority class"}, {"start_seconds": 193.97, "end_seconds": 198.77, "text": "performance. The distinction is simple."}, {"start_seconds": 196.77, "end_seconds": 201.57, "text": "K-fold ensures every point becomes"}, {"start_seconds": 198.77, "end_seconds": 204.09, "text": "validation exactly once. Stratified"}, {"start_seconds": 201.57, "end_seconds": 205.81, "text": "K-fold adds class ratio preservation to"}, {"start_seconds": 204.09, "end_seconds": 207.85, "text": "that rotation."}, {"start_seconds": 205.81, "end_seconds": 210.33, "text": "For imbalanced classification, use"}, {"start_seconds": 207.85, "end_seconds": 211.69, "text": "stratified folds so the validation sets"}, {"start_seconds": 210.33, "end_seconds": 214.33, "text": "represent the data sets class"}, {"start_seconds": 211.69, "end_seconds": 216.57, "text": "proportions. For temporal data, use"}, {"start_seconds": 214.33, "end_seconds": 218.21, "text": "time-ordered splits instead because"}, {"start_seconds": 216.57, "end_seconds": 220.13, "text": "random splitting can leak future"}, {"start_seconds": 218.21, "end_seconds": 222.37, "text": "information into training."}, {"start_seconds": 220.13, "end_seconds": 224.77, "text": "For binary classification, the confusion"}, {"start_seconds": 222.37, "end_seconds": 226.81, "text": "matrix is the foundation. Begin with"}, {"start_seconds": 224.77, "end_seconds": 228.73, "text": "what actually happened, then compare it"}, {"start_seconds": 226.81, "end_seconds": 230.97, "text": "with the prediction. An actually"}, {"start_seconds": 228.73, "end_seconds": 233.81, "text": "positive example predicted positive is a"}, {"start_seconds": 230.97, "end_seconds": 235.97, "text": "true positive or TP. An actually"}, {"start_seconds": 233.81, "end_seconds": 238.61, "text": "positive example predicted negative is a"}, {"start_seconds": 235.97, "end_seconds": 240.53, "text": "false negative or FN."}, {"start_seconds": 238.61, "end_seconds": 243.85, "text": "An actually negative example predicted"}, {"start_seconds": 240.53, "end_seconds": 245.65, "text": "negative is a true negative, or TN. An"}, {"start_seconds": 243.85, "end_seconds": 248.97, "text": "actually negative example predicted"}, {"start_seconds": 245.65, "end_seconds": 250.93, "text": "positive is a false positive, or FP."}, {"start_seconds": 248.97, "end_seconds": 252.77, "text": "These four counts make model behavior"}, {"start_seconds": 250.93, "end_seconds": 254.57, "text": "visible before they are compressed into"}, {"start_seconds": 252.77, "end_seconds": 257.73, "text": "a single metric."}, {"start_seconds": 254.57, "end_seconds": 259.89, "text": "Accuracy is TP + TN divided by all four"}, {"start_seconds": 257.73, "end_seconds": 262.41, "text": "counts, so it reports the fraction of"}, {"start_seconds": 259.89, "end_seconds": 264.13, "text": "correct predictions. But that aggregate"}, {"start_seconds": 262.41, "end_seconds": 265.17, "text": "can hide complete minority class"}, {"start_seconds": 264.13, "end_seconds": 267.09, "text": "failure."}, {"start_seconds": 265.17, "end_seconds": 269.81, "text": "Reporting the confusion matrix counts"}, {"start_seconds": 267.09, "end_seconds": 271.61, "text": "alongside derived metrics prevents class"}, {"start_seconds": 269.81, "end_seconds": 273.09, "text": "imbalance from disappearing behind a"}, {"start_seconds": 271.61, "end_seconds": 275.49, "text": "high score."}, {"start_seconds": 273.09, "end_seconds": 277.57, "text": "The matrix also connects each metric to"}, {"start_seconds": 275.49, "end_seconds": 279.13, "text": "a specific type of mistake, rather than"}, {"start_seconds": 277.57, "end_seconds": 281.13, "text": "treating performance as one"}, {"start_seconds": 279.13, "end_seconds": 283.53, "text": "undifferentiated number."}, {"start_seconds": 281.13, "end_seconds": 285.97, "text": "Precision, recall, and F1 answer"}, {"start_seconds": 283.53, "end_seconds": 289.09, "text": "different questions. Precision is TP"}, {"start_seconds": 285.97, "end_seconds": 291.17, "text": "divided by TP + FP. Among everything"}, {"start_seconds": 289.09, "end_seconds": 293.49, "text": "predicted positive, what fraction was"}, {"start_seconds": 291.17, "end_seconds": 295.73, "text": "actually positive? Use it when false"}, {"start_seconds": 293.49, "end_seconds": 298.89, "text": "positives are costly, such as a spam"}, {"start_seconds": 295.73, "end_seconds": 302.53, "text": "filter marking real email as spam."}, {"start_seconds": 298.89, "end_seconds": 304.77, "text": "Recall is TP divided by TP + FN. Among"}, {"start_seconds": 302.53, "end_seconds": 306.85, "text": "all actual positives, what fraction did"}, {"start_seconds": 304.77, "end_seconds": 309.05, "text": "the model catch? Use it when false"}, {"start_seconds": 306.85, "end_seconds": 310.89, "text": "negatives are costly, such as cancer"}, {"start_seconds": 309.05, "end_seconds": 313.37, "text": "screening missing a tumor."}, {"start_seconds": 310.89, "end_seconds": 315.69, "text": "F1 is two times precision times recall"}, {"start_seconds": 313.37, "end_seconds": 317.69, "text": "divided by their sum. It's the harmonic"}, {"start_seconds": 315.69, "end_seconds": 319.97, "text": "mean, balancing both measures when"}, {"start_seconds": 317.69, "end_seconds": 321.85, "text": "neither clearly dominates."}, {"start_seconds": 319.97, "end_seconds": 324.37, "text": "Metric selection must follow the task"}, {"start_seconds": 321.85, "end_seconds": 326.77, "text": "cost. Optimizing accuracy when recall"}, {"start_seconds": 324.37, "end_seconds": 329.33, "text": "matters can reward the wrong behavior."}, {"start_seconds": 326.77, "end_seconds": 332.25, "text": "On imbalanced classification, precision,"}, {"start_seconds": 329.33, "end_seconds": 334.81, "text": "recall, F1, or AUC ROC reveal"}, {"start_seconds": 332.25, "end_seconds": 336.73, "text": "information that accuracy can conceal."}, {"start_seconds": 334.81, "end_seconds": 339.37, "text": "Always connect the chosen score back to"}, {"start_seconds": 336.73, "end_seconds": 341.25, "text": "FP and FN costs, then report the"}, {"start_seconds": 339.37, "end_seconds": 342.57, "text": "underlying confusion matrix counts"}, {"start_seconds": 341.25, "end_seconds": 344.49, "text": "beside it."}, {"start_seconds": 342.57, "end_seconds": 347.05, "text": "AUC ROC evaluates ranking across"}, {"start_seconds": 344.49, "end_seconds": 349.09, "text": "classification thresholds. The ROC curve"}, {"start_seconds": 347.05, "end_seconds": 350.77, "text": "plots true positive rate against false"}, {"start_seconds": 349.09, "end_seconds": 353.37, "text": "positive rate while the threshold"}, {"start_seconds": 350.77, "end_seconds": 355.45, "text": "changes. Its area summarizes how well"}, {"start_seconds": 353.37, "end_seconds": 357.45, "text": "the model ranks positive examples above"}, {"start_seconds": 355.45, "end_seconds": 361.29, "text": "negative examples, regardless of the"}, {"start_seconds": 357.45, "end_seconds": 364.17, "text": "particular cutoff. An AUC of 0.5 means"}, {"start_seconds": 361.29, "end_seconds": 366.25, "text": "random guessing. An AUC of 1 means"}, {"start_seconds": 364.17, "end_seconds": 368.41, "text": "perfect separation."}, {"start_seconds": 366.25, "end_seconds": 369.86, "text": "That threshold independence is useful,"}, {"start_seconds": 368.42, "end_seconds": 372.25, "text": "but it doesn't remove the need to"}, {"start_seconds": 369.86, "end_seconds": 374.94, "text": "inspect the operating threshold. For"}, {"start_seconds": 372.25, "end_seconds": 376.42, "text": "rare event detection, ROC AUC alone can"}, {"start_seconds": 374.94, "end_seconds": 379.21, "text": "look strong while precision at the"}, {"start_seconds": 376.42, "end_seconds": 381.62, "text": "chosen threshold is unusable. So, use"}, {"start_seconds": 379.21, "end_seconds": 383.09, "text": "AUC ROC to evaluate ranking, then"}, {"start_seconds": 381.62, "end_seconds": 385.98, "text": "examine the threshold dependent"}, {"start_seconds": 383.1, "end_seconds": 387.42, "text": "confusion matrix, precision, and recall"}, {"start_seconds": 385.98, "end_seconds": 389.02, "text": "for the decision the system will"}, {"start_seconds": 387.42, "end_seconds": 391.1, "text": "actually make."}, {"start_seconds": 389.01, "end_seconds": 393.5, "text": "The curve and the operating point answer"}, {"start_seconds": 391.1, "end_seconds": 395.18, "text": "related but different questions."}, {"start_seconds": 393.5, "end_seconds": 397.98, "text": "Regression metrics measure prediction"}, {"start_seconds": 395.18, "end_seconds": 399.54, "text": "error without classification counts. MSE"}, {"start_seconds": 397.98, "end_seconds": 402.02, "text": "takes the mean of squared differences"}, {"start_seconds": 399.54, "end_seconds": 403.7, "text": "between true and predicted values."}, {"start_seconds": 402.01, "end_seconds": 406.21, "text": "Squaring makes large errors grow"}, {"start_seconds": 403.69, "end_seconds": 409.06, "text": "quadratically, so MSE is sensitive to"}, {"start_seconds": 406.21, "end_seconds": 411.89, "text": "outliers. RMSE is the square root of"}, {"start_seconds": 409.06, "end_seconds": 414.18, "text": "MSE. It keeps the same sensitivity, but"}, {"start_seconds": 411.89, "end_seconds": 416.81, "text": "returns to the target variable's units,"}, {"start_seconds": 414.18, "end_seconds": 419.62, "text": "which makes interpretation easier."}, {"start_seconds": 416.81, "end_seconds": 421.65, "text": "MAE takes the mean absolute difference."}, {"start_seconds": 419.62, "end_seconds": 424.38, "text": "It treats errors linearly and is more"}, {"start_seconds": 421.65, "end_seconds": 425.93, "text": "robust to outliers than MSE, making it a"}, {"start_seconds": 424.38, "end_seconds": 428.62, "text": "better choice for outlier heavy"}, {"start_seconds": 425.94, "end_seconds": 430.57, "text": "regression. R squared compares residual"}, {"start_seconds": 428.62, "end_seconds": 433.1, "text": "error with the total variation around"}, {"start_seconds": 430.57, "end_seconds": 434.5, "text": "the target mean. An R squared of one is"}, {"start_seconds": 433.1, "end_seconds": 436.78, "text": "perfect."}, {"start_seconds": 434.5, "end_seconds": 438.89, "text": "A value of zero means the model is no"}, {"start_seconds": 436.77, "end_seconds": 440.65, "text": "better than always predicting the mean,"}, {"start_seconds": 438.89, "end_seconds": 442.81, "text": "and it can be negative when the model is"}, {"start_seconds": 440.65, "end_seconds": 444.77, "text": "worse than that baseline. The right"}, {"start_seconds": 442.81, "end_seconds": 446.62, "text": "metric depends on which error behavior"}, {"start_seconds": 444.77, "end_seconds": 448.25, "text": "matters for the task."}, {"start_seconds": 446.62, "end_seconds": 450.18, "text": "Learning curves plot training and"}, {"start_seconds": 448.25, "end_seconds": 452.62, "text": "validation scores against training set"}, {"start_seconds": 450.18, "end_seconds": 454.74, "text": "size. Their shape diagnoses whether the"}, {"start_seconds": 452.62, "end_seconds": 456.89, "text": "model suffers from high bias or high"}, {"start_seconds": 454.74, "end_seconds": 459.01, "text": "variance. With high bias or"}, {"start_seconds": 456.89, "end_seconds": 461.45, "text": "underfitting, both curves converge to a"}, {"start_seconds": 459.01, "end_seconds": 463.33, "text": "low score. Adding more data won't solve"}, {"start_seconds": 461.45, "end_seconds": 465.33, "text": "that pattern. The lesson calls for a"}, {"start_seconds": 463.33, "end_seconds": 467.41, "text": "more complex model."}, {"start_seconds": 465.33, "end_seconds": 468.89, "text": "With high variance or overfitting, the"}, {"start_seconds": 467.42, "end_seconds": 471.25, "text": "training score is high while the"}, {"start_seconds": 468.89, "end_seconds": 473.17, "text": "validation score is much lower. The"}, {"start_seconds": 471.25, "end_seconds": 475.3, "text": "large gap shows that performance isn't"}, {"start_seconds": 473.18, "end_seconds": 477.5, "text": "transferring well to unseen data, and"}, {"start_seconds": 475.3, "end_seconds": 480.38, "text": "adding more data should help. Read both"}, {"start_seconds": 477.5, "end_seconds": 482.69, "text": "the level and the gap. Two low converged"}, {"start_seconds": 480.38, "end_seconds": 484.62, "text": "curves indicate underfitting."}, {"start_seconds": 482.69, "end_seconds": 486.69, "text": "A high training curve separated from a"}, {"start_seconds": 484.62, "end_seconds": 487.89, "text": "lower validation curve indicates"}, {"start_seconds": 486.69, "end_seconds": 490.14, "text": "overfitting."}, {"start_seconds": 487.89, "end_seconds": 492.42, "text": "A training score alone can't reveal this"}, {"start_seconds": 490.14, "end_seconds": 494.3, "text": "distinction because it shows fit on seen"}, {"start_seconds": 492.42, "end_seconds": 495.82, "text": "examples, not whether that fit"}, {"start_seconds": 494.3, "end_seconds": 498.1, "text": "generalizes."}, {"start_seconds": 495.82, "end_seconds": 500.82, "text": "Validation curves change the horizontal"}, {"start_seconds": 498.1, "end_seconds": 502.86, "text": "axis. Instead of training set size, they"}, {"start_seconds": 500.82, "end_seconds": 504.74, "text": "plot training and validation scores"}, {"start_seconds": 502.86, "end_seconds": 507.22, "text": "against a hyperparameter."}, {"start_seconds": 504.74, "end_seconds": 509.34, "text": "At low complexity, both scores are low,"}, {"start_seconds": 507.22, "end_seconds": 511.54, "text": "the model is underfitting. At the right"}, {"start_seconds": 509.34, "end_seconds": 513.18, "text": "complexity, both scores are high and"}, {"start_seconds": 511.54, "end_seconds": 515.14, "text": "close together."}, {"start_seconds": 513.18, "end_seconds": 517.18, "text": "At high complexity, the training score"}, {"start_seconds": 515.14, "end_seconds": 519.82, "text": "remains high while the validation score"}, {"start_seconds": 517.18, "end_seconds": 521.94, "text": "drops, revealing overfitting. The"}, {"start_seconds": 519.82, "end_seconds": 524.62, "text": "optimal hyperparameter value is where"}, {"start_seconds": 521.94, "end_seconds": 526.34, "text": "validation performance peaks. This curve"}, {"start_seconds": 524.62, "end_seconds": 528.9, "text": "turns tuning into an observable"}, {"start_seconds": 526.34, "end_seconds": 531.3, "text": "trade-off between insufficient capacity"}, {"start_seconds": 528.9, "end_seconds": 533.7, "text": "and excessive fit. But the decision must"}, {"start_seconds": 531.3, "end_seconds": 534.94, "text": "remain inside training and validation"}, {"start_seconds": 533.7, "end_seconds": 537.06, "text": "data."}, {"start_seconds": 534.94, "end_seconds": 539.22, "text": "Once a hyperparameter is chosen, the"}, {"start_seconds": 537.06, "end_seconds": 541.66, "text": "untouched test set is used only for the"}, {"start_seconds": 539.22, "end_seconds": 543.46, "text": "final report. Looking at test results"}, {"start_seconds": 541.66, "end_seconds": 545.1, "text": "during this search contaminates the"}, {"start_seconds": 543.46, "end_seconds": 546.9, "text": "final estimate."}, {"start_seconds": 545.1, "end_seconds": 549.3, "text": "The regression implementation mirrors"}, {"start_seconds": 546.9, "end_seconds": 551.58, "text": "the definitions directly. The MSE"}, {"start_seconds": 549.3, "end_seconds": 554.74, "text": "function averages squared residuals."}, {"start_seconds": 551.58, "end_seconds": 556.34, "text": "RMSE applies math sqrt to that result"}, {"start_seconds": 554.74, "end_seconds": 559.26, "text": "instead of creating a separate error"}, {"start_seconds": 556.34, "end_seconds": 561.82, "text": "calculation. MAE averages absolute"}, {"start_seconds": 559.26, "end_seconds": 564.14, "text": "residuals. R squared computes the target"}, {"start_seconds": 561.82, "end_seconds": 566.5, "text": "mean, the residual sum of squares, and"}, {"start_seconds": 564.14, "end_seconds": 568.42, "text": "the total sum of squares, then returns 1"}, {"start_seconds": 566.5, "end_seconds": 570.62, "text": "minus their ratio."}, {"start_seconds": 568.42, "end_seconds": 572.5, "text": "The highlighted return lines expose the"}, {"start_seconds": 570.62, "end_seconds": 574.98, "text": "core equations without hiding them"}, {"start_seconds": 572.5, "end_seconds": 577.02, "text": "behind a library call. There's also an"}, {"start_seconds": 574.98, "end_seconds": 579.62, "text": "explicit guard for a total sum of"}, {"start_seconds": 577.02, "end_seconds": 582.14, "text": "squares equal to zero, returning zero"}, {"start_seconds": 579.62, "end_seconds": 584.06, "text": "instead of dividing by zero."}, {"start_seconds": 582.14, "end_seconds": 586.62, "text": "These from scratch functions make metric"}, {"start_seconds": 584.06, "end_seconds": 589.14, "text": "behavior inspectable. Squared errors"}, {"start_seconds": 586.62, "end_seconds": 591.02, "text": "amplify large misses, absolute errors"}, {"start_seconds": 589.14, "end_seconds": 592.82, "text": "remain linear, and R squared is"}, {"start_seconds": 591.02, "end_seconds": 593.78, "text": "evaluated relative to predicting the"}, {"start_seconds": 592.82, "end_seconds": 595.54, "text": "mean."}, {"start_seconds": 593.78, "end_seconds": 597.1, "text": "The library workflow can add more"}, {"start_seconds": 595.54, "end_seconds": 599.26, "text": "scoring options and pipeline"}, {"start_seconds": 597.1, "end_seconds": 600.42, "text": "integration, but the definitions remain"}, {"start_seconds": 599.26, "end_seconds": 602.06, "text": "the same."}, {"start_seconds": 600.42, "end_seconds": 604.7, "text": "Several evaluation failures can"}, {"start_seconds": 602.06, "end_seconds": 606.54, "text": "invalidate an otherwise correct model."}, {"start_seconds": 604.7, "end_seconds": 608.7, "text": "Don't fit a scalar on the full data set"}, {"start_seconds": 606.54, "end_seconds": 611.46, "text": "before splitting. That leaks information"}, {"start_seconds": 608.7, "end_seconds": 613.98, "text": "across the boundary. Split first, then"}, {"start_seconds": 611.46, "end_seconds": 615.66, "text": "pre-process. Don't use a feature derived"}, {"start_seconds": 613.98, "end_seconds": 618.46, "text": "from the target, and don't include"}, {"start_seconds": 615.66, "end_seconds": 620.46, "text": "future data when predicting the past."}, {"start_seconds": 618.46, "end_seconds": 623.5, "text": "Don't trust accuracy on an imbalanced"}, {"start_seconds": 620.46, "end_seconds": 626.3, "text": "data set. When 99% of transactions are"}, {"start_seconds": 623.5, "end_seconds": 629.1, "text": "legitimate and 1% are fraud, always"}, {"start_seconds": 626.3, "end_seconds": 630.34, "text": "predicting legitimate still gets 99%"}, {"start_seconds": 629.1, "end_seconds": 632.62, "text": "accuracy."}, {"start_seconds": 630.34, "end_seconds": 635.06, "text": "Don't optimize RMSE for heavy outlier"}, {"start_seconds": 632.62, "end_seconds": 636.22, "text": "data when MAE better matches the error"}, {"start_seconds": 635.06, "end_seconds": 638.34, "text": "behavior."}, {"start_seconds": 636.22, "end_seconds": 640.38, "text": "Don't use ordinary random folds when"}, {"start_seconds": 638.34, "end_seconds": 642.18, "text": "imbalanced validation sets need"}, {"start_seconds": 640.38, "end_seconds": 644.46, "text": "stratification."}, {"start_seconds": 642.18, "end_seconds": 646.86, "text": "Don't inspect test performance, adjust"}, {"start_seconds": 644.46, "end_seconds": 649.34, "text": "thresholds or hyperparameters, and call"}, {"start_seconds": 646.86, "end_seconds": 651.86, "text": "the next result final. Every adjustment"}, {"start_seconds": 649.34, "end_seconds": 653.42, "text": "overfits decisions to the test set. And"}, {"start_seconds": 651.86, "end_seconds": 655.38, "text": "don't compare candidates on different"}, {"start_seconds": 653.42, "end_seconds": 658.02, "text": "folds, splits, or pre-processing"}, {"start_seconds": 655.38, "end_seconds": 660.74, "text": "pipelines because evaluation noise then"}, {"start_seconds": 658.02, "end_seconds": 662.34, "text": "becomes confounded with model choice."}, {"start_seconds": 660.74, "end_seconds": 664.42, "text": "Before promoting a model, run a"}, {"start_seconds": 662.34, "end_seconds": 666.54, "text": "disciplined review gate. Match the"}, {"start_seconds": 664.42, "end_seconds": 668.78, "text": "primary metric to the task cost."}, {"start_seconds": 666.54, "end_seconds": 670.94, "text": "Precision for expensive false positives,"}, {"start_seconds": 668.78, "end_seconds": 673.98, "text": "recall for expensive false negatives,"}, {"start_seconds": 670.94, "end_seconds": 677.14, "text": "MAE for outlier-heavy regression, and F1"}, {"start_seconds": 673.98, "end_seconds": 679.3, "text": "or PR AUC for imbalanced classification."}, {"start_seconds": 677.14, "end_seconds": 681.38, "text": "Confirm that tuning used only training"}, {"start_seconds": 679.3, "end_seconds": 683.5, "text": "and validation data, and that the test"}, {"start_seconds": 681.38, "end_seconds": 685.46, "text": "set was touched once."}, {"start_seconds": 683.5, "end_seconds": 687.7, "text": "Use stratified folds for imbalanced"}, {"start_seconds": 685.46, "end_seconds": 689.98, "text": "classification and time-ordered splits"}, {"start_seconds": 687.7, "end_seconds": 692.58, "text": "for temporal data. Report confusion"}, {"start_seconds": 689.98, "end_seconds": 694.38, "text": "matrix counts beside derived metrics."}, {"start_seconds": 692.58, "end_seconds": 696.9, "text": "Compare every candidate on identical"}, {"start_seconds": 694.38, "end_seconds": 699.02, "text": "folds and pre-processing pipelines."}, {"start_seconds": 696.9, "end_seconds": 701.18, "text": "Finally, check the selected model"}, {"start_seconds": 699.02, "end_seconds": 702.9, "text": "against the current production baseline."}, {"start_seconds": 701.18, "end_seconds": 704.86, "text": "Promotion should be blocked when the"}, {"start_seconds": 702.9, "end_seconds": 708.02, "text": "registered evaluation pass rate"}, {"start_seconds": 704.86, "end_seconds": 709.7, "text": "regresses beyond the allowed threshold."}, {"start_seconds": 708.02, "end_seconds": 711.82, "text": "This gate makes performance evidence"}, {"start_seconds": 709.7, "end_seconds": 713.7, "text": "comparable, exposes hidden class"}, {"start_seconds": 711.82, "end_seconds": 715.74, "text": "failures, and keeps a measurable"}, {"start_seconds": 713.7, "end_seconds": 717.38, "text": "regression from being shipped merely"}, {"start_seconds": 715.74, "end_seconds": 718.66, "text": "because one aggregate score looked"}, {"start_seconds": 717.38, "end_seconds": 720.86, "text": "attractive."}, {"start_seconds": 718.66, "end_seconds": 723.46, "text": "The central rule is simple. Measurement"}, {"start_seconds": 720.86, "end_seconds": 725.9, "text": "defines whether a model deserves trust."}, {"start_seconds": 723.46, "end_seconds": 728.26, "text": "Protect the test set, rotate validation"}, {"start_seconds": 725.9, "end_seconds": 730.5, "text": "with k-fold cross-validation, preserve"}, {"start_seconds": 728.26, "end_seconds": 732.18, "text": "class ratios with stratification, and"}, {"start_seconds": 730.5, "end_seconds": 735.42, "text": "choose metrics that reflect the real"}, {"start_seconds": 732.18, "end_seconds": 736.78, "text": "cost of FP, FN, outliers, and ranking"}, {"start_seconds": 735.42, "end_seconds": 738.66, "text": "errors."}, {"start_seconds": 736.78, "end_seconds": 741.18, "text": "Use learning curves to separate high"}, {"start_seconds": 738.66, "end_seconds": 743.26, "text": "bias from high variance, validation"}, {"start_seconds": 741.18, "end_seconds": 745.3, "text": "curves to select complexity, and"}, {"start_seconds": 743.26, "end_seconds": 747.3, "text": "identical evaluation pipelines to"}, {"start_seconds": 745.3, "end_seconds": 749.7, "text": "compare candidates fairly."}, {"start_seconds": 747.3, "end_seconds": 751.62, "text": "Accuracy alone is never a substitute for"}, {"start_seconds": 749.7, "end_seconds": 754.3, "text": "understanding the confusion matrix,"}, {"start_seconds": 751.62, "end_seconds": 756.22, "text": "especially with imbalanced data."}, {"start_seconds": 754.3, "end_seconds": 758.22, "text": "A strong evaluation process doesn't"}, {"start_seconds": 756.22, "end_seconds": 760.9, "text": "merely produce a score. It prevents"}, {"start_seconds": 758.22, "end_seconds": 762.66, "text": "leakage, exposes failure modes, and"}, {"start_seconds": 760.9, "end_seconds": 763.9, "text": "blocks measurable regressions before"}, {"start_seconds": 762.66, "end_seconds": 765.94, "text": "promotion."}, {"start_seconds": 763.9, "end_seconds": 767.94, "text": "Subscribe for the next AI platform"}, {"start_seconds": 765.94, "end_seconds": 770.1, "text": "engineering lesson and carry this"}, {"start_seconds": 767.94, "end_seconds": 774.18, "text": "evaluation discipline into every model"}, {"start_seconds": 770.1, "end_seconds": 774.18, "text": "you build, compare, and review."}]}